{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Partners and Cheek to Cheek feel like natural next choices because polished vocals, duets, and orchestral arrangements connect with what I enjoy in Stages and the Downton Abbey music.",
    "Loved Me Back to Life appeals because expressive ballads and strong melodic singing fit my interest in albums such as Lead With Your Heart."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Christmas albums connect with past listening, but their seasonal themes do not suit what I want to hear now, even when the vocal harmonies appeal.",
    "Traveller and 1989 offer sounds I am less drawn to right now: rootsier country and bright contemporary pop feel further from the relaxed, orchestral listening I currently prefer."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My earlier Christmas listening seems to have been treated as an ongoing desire for seasonal music.",
    "My interest in some country and vocal albums seems to have been stretched too broadly; a shared style or strong singer alone does not make an album my next choice."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My most recent classical listening suggests that a relaxed mood and orchestral accompaniment matter more to me right now.",
    "I distinguish between enjoying an expressive singer and wanting that album today: 25 appeals, but I would currently choose something closer to orchestral vocal music."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in expressive singing but give past seasonal and country listening more weight than my current preference for relaxed, orchestral music."
}"}
